torrent - ttywm on wayland
==========================
The same windows as ttywm, in frames drawn with the console's font:

	┌─[ firefox ]──────────────[x]┐
	│                             │
	└─────────────────────────────┘

but without the tty behind them: a wallpaper or a plain colour instead.
New windows type their border in, closed ones type it away.

The bottom line shows the network, volume, battery, date, time and which tty
you're on. Click the volume to mute, scroll on it to change it, click the
network to set up wifi. Notifications come up in the top right corner.

One C file on wlroots 0.19. X11 programs work through xwayland.
Needs foot for the terminal and fuzzel for the apps menu, or whatever you set.

Install
-------
	make
	sudo make install

then pick Torrent on your login screen, or run torrent-session from a console.

Settings
--------
Everything is in ~/.config/torrent/config, made the first time torrent starts.
It's the same plain words as ttywm's, and a few more:

	wallpaper = ~/pictures/sea.png
	keyboard layout = de
	tap to click = on
	window firefox = tty 2

Change a line and save: torrent picks it up straight away.

Keys
----
	Super+Return        terminal
	Super+d             apps menu
	Super+q             close window
	Super+Tab           next window
	Super+f             full screen
	Super+1..9          go to tty 1..9
	Super+Shift+1..9    send the window to tty 1..9
	Super+arrows        left half, right half, fill screen, put back
	Super+l             lock
	Super+Shift+e       log out
	Ctrl+Alt+F1..F12    the consoles

Click [x] to close, drag the title to move, drag the bottom right corner to
resize, or hold Super and drag with the left button to move, the right one to
resize.
